    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/12/mizuno-hyperwarp-pro-review-2026.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Full-length Enerzy XP foam is soft and bouncy with high stack (39 mm heel/33.5 mm forefoot) for strong long-run impact protection, but the heel/midfoot can feel clunky while the forefoot rides smooth with little flex.",
        "Responsiveness: The carbon-infused nylon plate adds snap and the foam returns energy, but the ride is less aggressive than true super racers and works better for tempo/long-distance efforts than sharp 5K-10K surges.",
        "Stability: Rigidity is high (shoe is not flexible), and the extreme lateral flare plus plate extension can help runners with lateral ankle instability, yet it can also cause a quick inward push and clunky transitions; there is no heel counter and lateral upper support is limited.",
        "Durability: Durability expectation is above average, and the Mizuno G3 outsole nubs provide strong road traction with likely solid outsole wear resistance."
      ]
    }
